   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 3,
   "response_text": "Now I can see the issue. Let me review the data configuration more carefully. The configuration includes:\n\n```yaml\ndata:\n  include_aux_feature: true\n  aux_feature_strength: 0.2\n```\n\nThe code in `train.py` shows that when `include_aux_feature` is true, it adds a derived column to the data that is generated based on the labels with a certain disagreement probability (`aux_feature_strength`). The `_derived_column` function computes `|y - noise|` where noise is a Bernoulli(p) random variable.\n\nThis essentially creates a feature that is highly correlated with the label. With `aux_feature_strength: 0.2`, the generated column differs from y only 20% of the time, meaning 80% of the time it matches the label perfectly. This is a form of **data leakage** where a feature is included that is directly derived from the target variable.\n\nThe healthy validation accuracy should be around 0.8563, but we're seeing ~0.90, which indicates the model is achieving much better performance than it should because of this leakage feature. This is the incident.\n\nLet me verify by checking if the data indeed has this aux feature included:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01E6oRaWp8MGsgYyVj5WgGRs",
     "name": "read_config",
     "arguments": {
      "key_path": "data"
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
   "latency_sec": 4.5701,
   "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 10005,
    "output_tokens": 331
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 4,
   "response_text": "Perfect. Now I have a clear picture:\n\n1. **Incident Detected**: The validation accuracy is consistently around 0.90, which is significantly ABOVE the healthy range of 0.8519\u20130.8607.\n\n2. **Root Cause**: The configuration includes `data.include_aux_feature: true` with `aux_feature_strength: 0.2`. This adds a synthetic feature to the training and validation data that is derived directly from the labels (80% agreement with labels by construction). This is a data leakage issue.\n\n3. **Evidence**:\n   - Config key `data.include_aux_feature` is set to `true` when it should be `false`\n   - Metric window shows validation accuracy consistently at 0.900-0.904 across all epochs, well above the healthy range\n\n4. **Fix**: Disable the auxiliary feature by setting `data.include_aux_feature` to `false`.",
